  "host": "EC2 c7i.4xlarge, Ubuntu 24.04, Intel Xeon Platinum 8488C. Each panel command ran in a fresh process under taskset -c 0-7, one logical CPU per physical core. Linux cgroup v2 memory.peak covers the entire process family including compilation and charged file cache. Sail timings are end-to-end process wall time.",
  "inputs": {
    "Flint": "ddalton/flint@8feba0c78f22e3ecdee0648c6b2897eac95ab1b4, lean/formal/LeanP1.tla and LeanP1Size3L1W3.cfg. See the linked 2026-11-22-checked-orbits.json for original upstream file locations. Each record carries SHA-256.",
    "Examples": "tlaplus/Examples@6a7b26a31c1a6aeec789b455e9bbfa3b3ad2728f. specifications/transaction_commit/{TCommit,TwoPhase}, specifications/CigaretteSmokers/CigaretteSmokers, specifications/SpecifyingSystems/AsynchronousInterface/AsynchInterface. Use the original .tla and .cfg files.",
    "peer": "ddalton/tla-mc@c8fce23493bb78fcd5405faf7b0653855db620ee. Compiler cache initially empty, shared across the edit sequence. The peer consumes the same pure transposition wrapper and CFG suffix and reports its own generated/representative counts. It does not issue a conjugacy proof or weighted census.",
    "edits": "Start at the published small source and CFG, then three unchanged runs. Prepend TRUE /\\ to Inv_CitationsLive. For growth, also replace barriers < MaxBarriers by barriers <= MaxBarriers in the Consume guard after s \\notin Readers /\\ w[s].pc = \"idle\". Revert the guard, then the property. Each run is a new process."
  },
  "build": {
    "Dive": "Rust 1.99.0, Linux x86_64, CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO=off CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_CODEGEN_UNITS=16 cargo build --release --locked -p dive-cli --bin dive and cargo build --release --locked -p dive-api --example orbit_graph --example symbolic_input; strip each executable. CPython 3.12.3, dd 0.6.0 for the finite proof.",
